  {
    "field": "argument_node.doc",
    "value": "VC dimension of homogeneous linear halfspaces: the Dudley upper bound.The class of homogeneous linear halfspaces x ↦ (0 < ⟨w, x⟩) in ℝⁿ has VC dimension at most n. This is the canonical instance of Dudley's bound (vcDim_signClass_le): the underlying function space is coordSpace n, of dimension n. (Cover 1965; Vapnik–Chervonenkis.)"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.pretty",
    "value": "∀ (n : ℕ), VCDim (Fin n → ℝ) (signClass (FLT.Halfspace.coordSpace n)) ≤ ↑n"
  },
  {
    "field": "dictionary_constant.name",
    "value": "FLT.Halfspace.coordSpace"
  },
  {
    "field": "dictionary_constant.name",
    "value": "VCDim"
  },
  {
    "field": "dictionary_constant.name",
    "value": "signClass"
  },
  {
